# Latin-only content → LTR (all locales)

## Rule (must)

Any control whose **content is Latin-only** must render **left-to-right** even when the app UI locale is RTL (`fa`, `ar`).

Applies to:
- **Credentials / identifiers:** email, username, password, API keys, tokens.
- **Numeric / parameter fields:** logistic `r`, `x0`, message bit length.
- **Latin URLs and phone numbers** when shown as values (About / contact / links).
- **Free-text message and extract result:** dynamic — LTR while Latin-only; RTL when Arabic/Persian/Hebrew is present; empty → follow UI locale.

Do **not** rely on app-wide `Directionality` / window RTL alone for these controls.

## Flutter (must)

- Resolve direction with `ContentTextDirection.resolve()` (`lib/core/ui/content_text_direction.dart`).
- **Input:** `DirectionalTextField` (not raw `TextField` / `TextFormField`).
  - Always LTR: `forceLatinLtr: true` (email, username, password, numbers).
- **Read-only Latin values:** `DirectionalLatinText` or `DirectionalSelectableText`.
- Password: `DirectionalTextField(forceLatinLtr: true, obscureText: true, ...)`.

```dart
// GOOD — email / username / password
DirectionalTextField(
  forceLatinLtr: true,
  controller: _emailCtrl,
  keyboardType: TextInputType.emailAddress,
)

DirectionalTextField(
  forceLatinLtr: true,
  obscureText: true,
  controller: _passwordCtrl,
)

// GOOD — displayed email or URL in About screen
DirectionalLatinText('karavi@ntk.ir', style: ...)
```

```dart
// BAD — inherits RTL from fa locale while typing "user@mail.com"
TextField(controller: _emailCtrl)
```

## WPF (must)

- Dynamic message/result: `ContentTextDirectionHelper.ApplyTo(TextBox, text)` on `TextChanged` or when text is assigned.
- Fixed Latin-only inputs: `Style="{StaticResource LatinInputTextBox}"` (`FlowDirection="LeftToRight"`).
- Latin display values (email, URL, phone): `FlowDirection="LeftToRight"` on the value `TextBlock` / `Hyperlink`, or `ContentTextDirectionHelper.ApplyTo(FrameworkElement, text, forceLatinLtr: true)`.

## Completion check

- New TextField/TextBox for email, username, password, numbers, or Latin-only values: direction wired before merge.
- Manual test in **fa** locale: type `user@mail.com` / `3.99` → LTR; type Persian → RTL; About email/URL values stay LTR.
